I reproduced a shutdown defect in the unchanged lifecycle code: a finite deleter that runs for 5.5 seconds outlives the default five-second wait, then aborts during normal CPython finalization. The control completes safely. I’ll record this as a MAJOR finding and mark F04/N5 partly closed; the bounded test in FIX2 uses `os._exit(0)`, which bypasses this failure.


