Scenario: a foreign-thread producer deleter enters under the actual admission protocol, then sleeps5.5s while releasing the GIL. The default5s atexit wait returns with still_in_flight=1. A module finalizer permits normal interpreter teardown to proceed while yielding the GIL. When the finite deleter wakes, CPython3.12 finalization terminates the foreign thread during GIL reacquisition. The forced unwind meets the catch-all/noexcept cleanup boundary and aborts the process. A warning or leaked manager cannot stop a callback already running.

